<!--
  deploy/dev reset smp

  DELETES THE SMP'S WHOLE VOLUME: world, .server cache, logs. On smp that world is Nordtal, which
  is in no repository and in no release.

  deploy/dev makes you TYPE THE SERVICE NAME BACK before it does anything - not "yes", the name -
  and that prompt is why this runs in the terminal. plugins/ is a directory on the host and
  survives. Nothing here weakens that guard; it only saves typing the command.

  Why this runs the way it does - the interpreter, the terminal, the working directory - is in
  .run/README.md, once, rather than in each of these thirty files.
-->
